# Database Interactions

When reading or writing data:

1. **Use Prisma** — never raw SQL or another ORM unless explicitly required.
2. **Wrap in try/catch** — every Prisma call must be inside try/catch; handle or rethrow with context.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
async findById(id: string) {
  try {
    return await this.prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { id } });
  } catch (error) {
    throw new InternalServerErrorException('Failed to fetch user', { cause: error });
  }
}
```

Inject `PrismaService`; do not instantiate Prisma clients directly in feature code.

## Ownership (no duplicate FKs)

Private queries must include the existing owner field (`teacherId` or `User.id`). Do **not** add a second user FK when one already exists (`Contract.teacherId`).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — scope with the existing owner
await this.prisma.contract.findUnique({ where: { id, teacherId: userId } });

// ❌ BAD — extra fk_user_id on Contract, or unscoped findUnique({ where: { id } })
```

Public catalogs (`Class`, `Institution`, `PricingMode`, `Status`) have no owner. See `saas-api.mdc`.
